1795387044095844	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-iv7	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-23g"}	blake3:IudN0MSDnuERhLvPT94EIEja1dSfxAPAWuzN9qtWzLY
1795387044154231	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1y5	{"field":"title","value":"M1.10.3 Package three pilot families, one per source, and record the authoring cost"}	blake3:dm42WLe1GsMvmySoxgUCpJ1jz2XZvXTtV7r_yYuvHxE
1795387044164685	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1y5	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nThe first packaged families set the cost estimate for the rest. The owner prefers a larger corpus where cost allows (notes/plan.evaluation.md §11), so the number of families M1.10.4 packages comes from what these three cost.\n\n# Do\nFrom the M1.10.2 candidate list, package one family from each source in the M1.10.1 format: a historical authorization CVE with its vulnerable and fixed release; a one-check mutation of an open-source multi-user application; and a RealWorld backend as a policy-decoy family (its reads are public by design). Before packaging, check each against the first oracle: the vulnerable build gives `true`, the fixed build does not, and the functional checks pass on both. For the policy decoy, the result is `true` and the declared rule refutes it. Record the hours each family took, by step.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Three packaged families, each with accounts, ground truth, fix and partial-fix variants and functional checks, each run through the harness from its package.\n- [ ] Authoring cost per family and per step is in the ledger, with a projected cost for the remaining families.\n- [ ] The implementing agent has had no access to them.\n\nNeeds the first oracle (M1.5) for the screening step. Write-side families wait for the second oracle (M1.10.5).\n\nOwner: not the implementing agent.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §12.2 (row M1.10); notes/plan.evaluation.md §5, §11.\n"}	blake3:E3lHTD3vmsiPjCof9EL_Smk38BHxTPXwNQiQsyB8zb8
1795387044165705	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1y5	{"field":"size","value":"m"}	blake3:MF7eMtl8ZZP8HfSV6T-USmw4zdXuYT1IdvcHDXxX0iE
1795387044185824	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-27p	{"description":"# Context\nMost of the Tier 1 corpus. The count comes from the pilot's cost (M1.10.3). Ten to twelve families in all, counting M1.10.5, is the floor, and more is better where cost allows.\n\n# Do\nPackage the chosen read-side families (cross-principal and unauthenticated reads, with fix and partial-fix cases) and the decoy families from the M1.10.2 list, in the M1.10.1 format. Screen each against the first oracle before packaging it. Once the list is chosen, create one child bone per family so that each family's cost and state is tracked on its own.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Each family has accounts, ground truth, fix and partial-fix variants and functional checks, and runs through the harness from its package.\n- [ ] Authoring cost per family is in the ledger.\n- [ ] The implementing agent has had no access to them.\n\nOwner: not the implementing agent.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.evaluation.md §5, §11.\n","kind":"task","labels":["eval","fixture","m1","separate-owner"],"parent":"bn-14c","size":"l","title":"M1.10.4 Package the remaining read-side and decoy families"}	blake3:69kicMRArOZmRinJYZ2dTVHREQ4KzYc_tM-Ru1gJZwY
1795387044213765	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-27p	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-1y5"}	blake3:ZnpN1Gmi0CKoeEZIkwXx62zH_IhBqmO7CF9i9DprOnI
1795387044242207	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3dv	{"description":"# Context\nWrite-side families (cross-principal and anonymous state changes, many of them from RealWorld backends) can be screened only against `web.forbidden-state-change.v1`, which ships in M2.1. The plan checks each candidate against a shipped oracle before packaging it (row M1.10), so these families cannot finish in M1. Before this bone, M1.10.3 claimed write violations while depending only on the first oracle.\n\n# Do\nOnce M2.1 is done, screen and package the write-side families from the M1.10.2 list. The vulnerable build gives `true` under the second oracle, the fixed build does not, and the functional checks pass on both.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Each write-side family is packaged in the M1.10.1 format with accounts, ground truth, fix and partial-fix variants and functional checks.\n- [ ] Authoring cost per family is in the ledger.\n- [ ] The implementing agent has had no access to them.\n\nOwner: not the implementing agent.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §6.6, §12.2 (row M1.10); notes/plan.evaluation.md §5.\n","kind":"task","labels":["eval","fixture","m1","separate-owner"],"parent":"bn-14c","size":"m","title":"M1.10.5 Package the write-side families once the second oracle ships"}	blake3:8Rqr-JIL8fL76IbmbnPl9jBx8Lvnoc03iostjoZNloQ
1795387044270112	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3dv	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-1y5"}	blake3:r6N3dixbs3CiJRTEZirXdDcvQQWC-OQEILKYsVoX3O8
1795387044298952	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3dv	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-lkm"}	blake3:nF031Hquf5k_R3AszivZrBAQjPCFQ4Zej5frT3jkLcU
1795387044331248	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2kf	{"description":"# Context\nM2.10 needs a fixed set. The trial ledger is frozen by family before the scored round, and families are added before freezing, not after seeing results (notes/plan.evaluation.md §11).\n\n# Do\n- Check the packaged set's coverage: every decoy class in the fixture catalog, real read and write violations, fix and partial-fix cases, and the tracks each family suits (discovery, supplied lead, negative, fix verification, recovery).\n- Check independence: the families differ in structure, not in names (the variation axes of M1.10.1), and the access record shows the implementing agent had no access.\n- Fingerprint the set and hand it to M2.10's trial ledger.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] A coverage table in which each gap is closed by a family or listed as a known gap.\n- [ ] The frozen set's fingerprint is recorded. Any later change is a new fingerprint.\n\nOwner: not the implementing agent.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.evaluation.md §5, §6, §11.\n","kind":"task","labels":["eval","fixture","m1","separate-owner"],"parent":"bn-14c","size":"s","title":"M1.10.6 Audit Tier 1 coverage and freeze the set"}	blake3:r0zxnXkH_7o8tTrywOeQ2PNV_TxGm8EFrW-AbIDRI5o
1795387044362774	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-2kf	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-27p"}	blake3:oaUKgvvW5vGa8cY2V9n5I2oXmudTb1D203K0AAffxJg
1795387044393658	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-2kf	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3dv"}	blake3:na83kTCYWwdbGwnyiHxUhVkgJhOAyicqtbvEf3xcyho
1795387075308624	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-9dy	{"description":"# Context\nThe M2 exit says the end-to-end scenario of plan §1.5 runs on real binaries. Before this bone, no bone owned that run. Each M2 package tests its own part. This one runs the parts together, the way an operator and an agent would, before M2.10 spends trial budget on them.\n\n# Do\nA scripted acceptance run on the development fixture with real binaries built from a clean checkout (`scourge`, `scourge-verify`, Teapot, Hallpass, Playpen and the shipped Investigation), through every row of §1.5: orient; explore with Teapot as two users; record a lead; import a Teapot finding; preview; verify; the three decoys; the dropped response; report, then `bundle check` in a clean environment; and retest after the fix switch. Assert each row's durable result. Run it once in shared custody and once in isolated custody with separate principals.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Every row of §1.5 produces the durable result its table names, in both tiers.\n- [ ] The record names the version of every binary and of Investigation, and the M2 goal links it at close.\n- [ ] It runs as a named qualification runner, apart from the fast suite (notes/plan.evaluation.md §13). A skipped step fails the run.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §1.5, §12.1; notes/plan.evaluation.md §13.\n","kind":"task","labels":["integration","m2","test"],"parent":"bn-i1o","size":"m","title":"M2.11 Run the §1.5 end-to-end scenario on real binaries, in both custody tiers"}	blake3:MWClPyXJ3E96hvhwpurGw3v3eAq-rLKsgmK7r8tP8uY
1795387075332312	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-9dy	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-2vj"}	blake3:m8PSwEvSgaqtHvA_DV80U_UZKIMX3o-QWyxlQ8q9m8M
